From: Richard-Yhn <richard-yhn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:34:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add a room-log endpoint so a client can read a group
 chat
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- `room-log { roomId, before?, limit? }` returns one page of room.log, newest
  page first, cursor by seq. `before` is the seq of the oldest line the caller
  already holds; `cursor` is null once the log is read to its start or the host
  has dropped those lines (it keeps ROOM_LOG_KEPT, reported as `kept`).
- Pure paging lives in src/host/room-log.js and is covered by
  test/room-log.test.js (9 cases), so the wiring in channel.js stays thin.
- A cut line keeps its stored head plus `length`, and `file-text` still fetches
  the whole text.
- Read-only: added to READS, so a host that only reads the team answers it.
- Unknown roomId answers bot/not-found instead of throwing.

Why: state carries only the last line of each room as `preview` — view()
destructures `log` away — so any client that is not this window has no way to
draw a group chat. The iOS client this was written for falls back to the web
view without this endpoint.
